                        "review": "In my opinion, the best and deepest of the idle game genre. It has near endless progression. You can play it a variety of ways, from checking in every few minutes to every few days, And it has full offline progression, so no need to keep it running in the background. If you like watching numbers get incrementally bigger, with progress actually feeling meaningful, this game is excellent.\r\n\r\nIt is, admittedly, a bit bloated. The sheer amount of content can be overwhelming. In the main game alone, there's your trainings, your creations, monuments, the divinity generator, might. And then there's pets, which are their whole own thing, and adventure is yet another thing entirely. And then there's all the other content you eventually unlock, the space dim machine, multiverses, RTI . . . it is a lot. It will take a decent amount more strategizing and game-knowledge than most other idle games.\r\n\r\n The final caveat is that it is very much an IDLE game. Do not expect to be making great leaps of progress in a couple of hours. It's been quite a while since I made my first climb through the gods, but I remember it taking several days to several weeks. And that is just the beginning. The challenges, of which there are dozens, many of which you'll want to complete 20-50 times, can take anywhere from a couple hours to a couple days, with the outlier (and completely optional) Arty challenge taking anywhere from several weeks to several months of real time. I have, as of writing this, nearly 2500 hours in the game, and countless more hours of offline progress and I am still in what is considered the early mid-game. If you're looking to 100% this, it is going to be the work of YEARS.\r\n\r\nAll that said, I definitely recommend it. It has brought me a great deal of joy over the years.",
